From f7535bdeac5f6cf9221de99453563b6f81750bee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lmore377 <jessica@corvuscollective.org>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 21:21:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] plat/amlogic: carthing-specific eFuse user-area base
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream's plat/amlogic/common/aml_efuse.c hardcodes EFUSE_BASE 0x140
as the start of the user-area within SCP-mediated eFuse reads. That
value matches some Amlogic reference designs but is wrong for the
Spotify Car Thing (S905D2, Toshiba THGBMNG5D1LBAIL eMMC + vendor SCP
firmware): reads at user_offset=18 (where the usid lives per
Spotify's user-area layout) return data ~96 bytes off, landing in the
mac_bt region.

Established empirically by scanning SCP eFuse offsets via u-boot's
`sm efuseread` and locating the known content (mac_bt OUI 30:e3:d6,
the ASCII serial, the f_serial date-code). usid backsolves to a
user-area base of 0x1a0.

Aftermath: `printenv serial#` in u-boot returns the per-unit eFuse
usid (matches what `adb get-serialno` reports on stock firmware),
and the same value lands as the iSerial USB gadget descriptor.

This needs an upstream story before submission — should probably be
a DT property (`amlogic,efuse-base`) read by the SCPI driver, since
different boards have different layouts. Logged here as a working
local patch; will revisit when porting to mainline kernel work.
---
 plat/amlogic/common/aml_efuse.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/amlogic/common/aml_efuse.c b/plat/amlogic/common/aml_efuse.c
index 00884eb..3c3b83c 100644
--- a/plat/amlogic/common/aml_efuse.c
+++ b/plat/amlogic/common/aml_efuse.c
@@ -8,7 +8,17 @@
 
 #include "aml_private.h"
 
-#define EFUSE_BASE	0x140
+/*
+ * EFUSE_BASE = 0x1a0 matches vendor BL31's convention on Spotify Car
+ * Thing (S905D2). Established empirically by scanning SCP eFuse offsets
+ * with `sm efuseread`: known content (mac_bt OUI 30:e3:d6, usid ASCII
+ * serial, f_serial date code) appears at SCP offsets 0x1a6, 0x1b2,
+ * 0x1c2 respectively — backsolves to user-area base 0x1a0 with the
+ * Spotify layout (offset 0 = mac, 6 = mac_bt, 12 = mac_wifi,
+ * 18 = usid, 34 = f_serial). Upstream default 0x140 is for a different
+ * Amlogic board; on this chip+SCP combo it returns data ~96 bytes off.
+ */
+#define EFUSE_BASE	0x1a0
 #define EFUSE_SIZE	0xC0
 
 uint64_t aml_efuse_read(void *dst, uint32_t offset, uint32_t size)
